\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Remark}
\title{How we formulate lifecycle accounting}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{compute}

\p{The scaling study behind \ref{ftip-001C} reports training tokens and
compute separately.}

\p{\citet{sec. 3}{hoffmann2022training} studies their allocation. We
therefore formulate separate cost coordinates.}

\p{Agentic and replay protocols also incur verifier, environment, storage,
and selection work. A training step, a generated rollout, and one second of
wall time are therefore different units.}

\p{The vector permits later cost models without hiding which conversion rates
or hardware assumptions they use.}
